msgstr "Only on the stars and their halos; the nebula keeps the overall saturation. In a refractor with a color camera, the halo of blue stars is red + blue (they focus away from green) and with high saturation it turns violet: 0.5–0.8 leaves them white, blue or orange according to their real color."

